```mermaid
flowchart LR
  R[Reference a name] --> L{Local binding?}
  L -- Yes --> U[Use it]
  L -- No --> E{Enclosing function binding?}
  E -- Yes --> U
  E -- No --> G{Current module global?}
  G -- Yes --> U
  G -- No --> B{Built-in name?}
  B -- Yes --> U
  B -- No --> N[NameError]
```

The path describes references. A binding operation such as assignment can classify the name as local before the function runs.

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A[Who owns the state?] --> C{Only one call?}
  C -- Yes --> L[Local variable]
  C -- No --> P{Small private state for nested functions?}
  P -- Yes --> N[Enclosing binding + nonlocal]
  P -- No --> O{Several operations or fields?}
  O -- Yes --> B[Dedicated object/component]
  O -- No --> G[Consider module state carefully]
```
